      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for google-osconfig-agent",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for google-osconfig-agent fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-61801: github.com/moby/sys/user: unbounded parsing of user and group database files can lead to denial of\n  service (bsc#1284870).\n- CVE-2026-78669: golang.org/x/net/http2: excessive CPU consumption from repeated initial window changes (bsc#1285283).\n- CVE-2026-95838: github.com/containerd/containerd: processing of certain image layers causes superlinear time\n  complexity in unpack handler and can lead to DoS (bsc#1285135).\n\nChanges for google-osconfig-agent:\n\n- Update to version 20261015.00\n * Add scalibr os benchmarks (#1044)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SLE-Micro-6.0-948",
        "title": "Patchnames"
